syntax:
template< class InputIt, class OutputIt >
OutputIt std::copy( InputIt first, InputIt last, OutputIt d_first );
// Implementation notes: 'first' and 'last' define the source range [first, last), which is iterated over. 'd_first' is the start of the destination range. The function returns an iterator to the element past the last element copied. Note that no checks are performed on the destination range size; if the distance between d_first and the end of the intended destination is less than the distance between first and last, undefined behavior occurs at runtime.
